<title>MALAYSIA: SQUASH-WOMEN'S WORLD TEAM CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SQUASH-WOMEN'S WORLD TEAM CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PETALING JAYA, Malaysia 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the</p>
<p>women's world team squash championships on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Pool A:</p>
<p>Australia beat South Africa 3-0</p>
<p>Michelle Martin beat Claire Nitch 9-0 9-4 4-9 2-9 9-6</p>
<p>Sarah Fitz-Gerald beat Chantal Clifton-Parks 9-3 9-4 9-0</p>
<p>Carol Owens beat Angelique Clifton-Parks 9-5 9-3 9-2</p>
<p>Germany beat United States 3-0</p>
<p>Sabine Schone beat Demer Holleran 9-2 9-1 9-1</p>
<p>Sabine Baum beat Ellie Pierce 9-2 9-5 9-0</p>
<p>Silke Bartel bet Alicia Mcconnell 9-5 2-9 10-8 9-5</p>
<p>Pool B:</p>
<p>England beat Netherlands 3-0</p>
<p>Cassie Jackman beat Vanessa Atkinson 9-4 9-6 8-10 8-10 9-2</p>
<p>Suzanne Horner beat Denise Sommers 9-2 9-1 9-4</p>
<p>Fiona Geaves bet Daphne Jegersma 9-1 9-0 9-1</p>
<p>New Zealand beat Egypt 3-0</p>
<p>Philippa Beams beat Salma Shabana 6-9 9-5 9-1 9-2</p>
<p>Leilani Marsh beat May Hegazy 9-0 9-1 9-0</p>
<p>Jade Wilson beat Heba Abu Ouf 9-3 9-6 9-6</p>
<p>Pool C:</p>
<p>Finland beat Canada 2-1 (Finnish names first)</p>
<p>Tuula Myllyniemi beat Heather Wallace 9-7 4-9 9-6 9-2</p>
<p>Nina Taimiaho beat Melanie Jens 9-0 9-6 9-6</p>
<p>Kia Paasivirta lost to Kelsey Souchereau 8-10 5-9 3-9</p>
<p>Ireland beat Malaysia 3-0</p>
<p>Aisling McArdle beat Leong Siu Lynn 9-4 9-2 9-6</p>
<p>Lousie Finnegan beat Kuan Choy Lin 9-3 9-7 10-8</p>
<p>Olivia French beat Carrie Yeo 5-9 10-9 9-3 9-3</p>
<p>Pool D:</p>
<p>France beat Hong Kong 2-1 (French names first)</p>
<p>Corinne Castets beat Dawn Olsen 9-5 8-10 9-3 9-3</p>
<p>Corinne Verzin lost to Rebecca Chiu 9-6 6-9 9-4 2-9 4-9</p>
<p>Laurence Brunier beat Iris Chung 9-6 9-0 9-2</p>
<p>Scotland beat Japan 3-0</p>
<p>Senga Macfie beat Yuko Kimura 9-0 9-1 9-1</p>
<p>Claire Waddell beat Miyuki Adachi 9-3 9-1 9-1</p>
<p>Wendy Maitland beat Misako Sugo 9-0 9-3 9-6</p>
<p>Pool E:</p>
<p>Denmark beat Brazil 2-1 (Danish names first)</p>
<p>Ellen Hamborg-Petersen lost to Flavia Roberts 4-9 9-10 6-9</p>
<p>Julie Dorn-Jensen beat Adriana Moura 4-9 9-4 9-1 9-3</p>
<p>Elsebeth Jensen beat Aline Laginestra 9-0 9-2 9-4</p>
<p>Spain beat Italy 3-0</p>
<p>Natalie Menen beat Teresa Beresford 10-8 9-7 9-0</p>
<p>Elisabet Sado beat Sonia Pasteris 9-5 9-4 9-0</p>
<p>Nuria Salvia beat Elena Cambi 9-0 9-3 9-2</p>
</text>
